        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-28T20:40:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No not a mistake. The password hashing is done in the SQL model now, not independently in a separate function. This prevents any \"Set password\" that is not hashed, meaning plain-text, in the DB and consolidates how we hash the password.\n\nchange_password_required is specific to saying \"hey this password was administratively changed and must be changed before next login\". See (above, copied here for visibility):\n\n    def _change_password_required(self, user):\n        if not CONF.security_compliance.change_password_upon_first_use:\n            return False\n        ignore_option \u003d user.get_resource_option(\n            options.IGNORE_CHANGE_PASSWORD_OPT.option_id)\n        return not (ignore_option and ignore_option.option_value is True)",
      "parentUuid": "ffe62b97_0e2f9e3f",
      "revId": "c283a0fcd4b57d165c5479ca04da1e014b2ab4c9",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
