    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ffe62b97_515b7e86",
        "filename": "releasenotes/notes/bug_1543048_and_1668503-7ead4e15faaab778.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 7353
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-23T22:24:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it may be worth while to spell out to folks that ALL users of the cloud will be forced to reset their passwords in order to ensure strong hashing within the PIKE cycle and that will need to be done before folks are able to upgrade to R. \n\nThis is assuming I\u0027m understanding the PR correctly.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "c283a0fcd4b57d165c5479ca04da1e014b2ab4c9",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ffe62b97_0305f713",
        "filename": "releasenotes/notes/bug_1543048_and_1668503-7ead4e15faaab778.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-28T20:40:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "User passwords that are not set after this code lands will continue to validate, just using the less secure hash. Passwords that are set after this code has landed (Pike) will use the new hash(ing).\n\nWe do not want to break users. The core of this code is to ensure users are not broken even if they do not change their passwords. If we were to go with a hard break, the patchset would have been much, much, much smaller.",
      "parentUuid": "ffe62b97_515b7e86",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "c283a0fcd4b57d165c5479ca04da1e014b2ab4c9",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ffe62b97_ab5019d6",
        "filename": "releasenotes/notes/bug_1543048_and_1668503-7ead4e15faaab778.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 5046
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-23T21:17:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From an operator perspective what happens if I don\u0027t do this last step? Is this a timing thing? Do I have to switch this back within X amount of time after I run my contract phase?",
      "revId": "c283a0fcd4b57d165c5479ca04da1e014b2ab4c9",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ffe62b97_f679682f",
        "filename": "releasenotes/notes/bug_1543048_and_1668503-7ead4e15faaab778.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 5046
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-23T21:31:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This has to be switched back to False after a deployment is running all Pike code and an admin has forced all users to reset their passwords, right?",
      "parentUuid": "ffe62b97_ab5019d6",
      "revId": "c283a0fcd4b57d165c5479ca04da1e014b2ab4c9",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ffe62b97_e616a149",
        "filename": "releasenotes/notes/bug_1543048_and_1668503-7ead4e15faaab778.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-28T20:40:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not even after all users have been forced to do a password change. Simply after all keystones are running pike code.\n\nOld passwords will continue to validate, full stop. \n\nWe cannot break users because a password wasn\u0027t reset. \n\nAn operator may require a password change, but that is on them, we do not have any such requirements in code.",
      "parentUuid": "ffe62b97_f679682f",
      "revId": "c283a0fcd4b57d165c5479ca04da1e014b2ab4c9",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ffe62b97_e6ea21d6",
        "filename": "releasenotes/notes/bug_1543048_and_1668503-7ead4e15faaab778.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-28T20:49:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In fact... we don\u0027t even have the contract migration implemented since we can\u0027t eliminate the column until Q (with a data migration as well) without breaking code.",
      "parentUuid": "ffe62b97_e616a149",
      "revId": "c283a0fcd4b57d165c5479ca04da1e014b2ab4c9",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ffe62b97_4b274d66",
        "filename": "releasenotes/notes/bug_1543048_and_1668503-7ead4e15faaab778.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 5046
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-23T21:17:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Might be worth noting here that administrators can force users to upgrade their passwords, which eludes to one possible way administrators can go about making that change happen.",
      "revId": "c283a0fcd4b57d165c5479ca04da1e014b2ab4c9",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ffe62b97_9ce8fd16",
        "filename": "releasenotes/notes/bug_1543048_and_1668503-7ead4e15faaab778.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 43,
      "author": {
        "id": 7353
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-23T22:24:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d also like to have this, or something like it, sent out as some form of a security advisory. When I force my users to reset their passwords they\u0027re going to ask why. Having an OSSA security advisory published to https://security.openstack.org/ossalist.html (or something similar) would likely make a lot of those questions go away while also providing my Product and C-Type folks a reason as to why we\u0027re forcing our users to do this.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 43,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "c283a0fcd4b57d165c5479ca04da1e014b2ab4c9",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
